BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Townies (or\, My Little Town): Special Stowe Screening
DTSTART:20260829T180000
DTEND:20260829T190000
DTSTAMP:20260829T154018Z
UID:55d5efa80a2013549aec5aaed6dabd@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:'Townies (or\, My Little Town)'\, the short film from Vermonte
 r Callum Adams\, will have a special screening in Stowe on Saturday August
  29th at 6pm at Stowe Cinema. The film is 22-minutes and will be followed 
 by a Q&A with writer/director Callum Adams. There will be a 7pm post-scree
 ning reception at Front Four Gallery for anyone that would like to attend.
  Tickets for the screening are $15 and will be sold at the door. We kindly
  ask that people RSVP ahead of the screening. Following its world premiere
  at the Oscar-qualifying HollyShorts Film Festival in LA\, 'Townies' pulls
  two people who share a resort town into a single tense encounter\, asking
  who really gets to call a place home. This is Adams’ directorial debut 
 and stars Maren Lord (Fear the Walking Dead) and Michel Gill (House of Car
 ds). The film is produced by Vermont filmmakers Mark Freeman and Brandon S
 t. Cyr of Kid Brother Pictures\, and is executive produced by three-time E
 mmy winner Tom Fontana. Content warning: Strong language and mature themes
 . Not suitable for children. For more info about the film\, you can read a
 n interview with Callum Adams for League of Filmmakers. Ticketing info: $1
 5\, Tickets will be sold at the door. Please RSVP to secure a spot. 454 Mo
 untain Road Stowe \, Vermont 05672 Submit An Event Find out what's happeni
