BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:VTIFF Screening of "Dilwale Dulhania Le Jayenge" (1995)
DTSTART:20260829T150000
DTEND:20260829T180000
DTSTAMP:20260829T154018Z
UID:a8f02c83b7a033e823452382fc39cc@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:On what could very well be a long hot summer day\, why not ste
 p into the air-condition and pass the afternoon enjoying one of the great 
 Bollywood musicals of all time. The longest-running film in the history of
  Indian cinema\, still screening at Mumbai’s Maratha Mandir cinema 30 ye
 ars after its release\, Dilwale Dulhania Le Jayenge—popularly referred t
 o as “DDLJ”—stars Shah Rukh Khan and Kajol as Raj and Simran\, two L
 ondoners who fall in love on a European backpacking holiday. But then—as
  film lovers often are—they are separated when Simran’s disapproving f
 ather ships the family off to Punjab\, but then reunited when headstrong R
 aj comes storming after her. Every inch of the ’Scope frame gets used in
  the riotously colorful musical numbers\, including the infectious\, bliss
 ed-out “Dilwale Dulhania Le Jayenge\,” in a film that fairly overflows
  with the exuberance\, charisma\, and showmanship that Bollywood at its be
 st can offer. The film was rapturously received on its release\, becoming 
 one of the highest-grossing Hindi films ever\, and winning a then-record 1
 0 Filmfare Awards (for excellence in Hindi cinema). If anything\, its lege
 nd has only grown since then. The Screening Room @VTIFF\n\nSources: Vermon
 t Public
LOCATION:60 Lake St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/vtiff-scre
 ening-of-dilwale-dulhania-le-jayenge-1995-26-08-2026-10-50-24
END:VEVENT
