SUMMARY:Braintree Bluegrass Brunch: Ida Mae Specker & Friends (feat. squar
 e dances called by Sarah Gibson)
DTSTART:20260830T100000
DTEND:20260830T150000
DTSTAMP:20260829T154018Z
UID:3dc8c3a969a848aa7bba10abcd0dd0@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Braintree Hill Meetinghouse Sunday\, August 30t
 h for live music\, bike rides\, food\, and family fun! Ida Mae Specker\, d
 aughter of John Specker\, brings Vermont’s folk traditions to life throu
 gh old-time fiddle music\, heartfelt vocals\, and intergenerational musici
 anship. Blending traditional and contemporary folk influences shaped by st
 orytelling\, community\, and place\, her performances create an intimate a
 nd powerful musical experience rooted in American folk tradition. Special 
 guest Sarah Gibson will get the audience moving with her square dance call
 ing\, perfectly complementing Ida’s spirited performance. Event Schedule
  10 AM: Mountain bike ride with Ridgeline Outdoor Collective 11 AM: Ground
 s open 12–3 PM: Live music Food\, drink\, and select craft vendors will 
 be on site. Please leave pets at home.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
